  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows multiprofile RNA with avgpool and PCA (config_002, accuracy 0.591, F1 0.573) clearly outperforms singleprofile PCA RNA (config_001, accuracy 0.485, F1 0.464), while image-only ResNet is weak (config_010, accuracy 0.208). The key uncertainty is whether the multiprofile gain is already captured by simple average pooling or whether transformer aggregation would further improve the representation. config_003 changes only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping rna_only, multiprofile, and pca_n2000 fixed, so it cleanly isolates the aggregation effect. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the strongest current direction with a low-confound comparison and provides high-leverage information for choosing aggregation in later multimodal settings."
}

